# Optional-menu SPACE stalls: bounded read-only diagnosis

Current source inspection: 2026-09-25T07:18:49.092437+00:00. No interpreter launched, no input sent to any game, no process attached/stopped, no app or shared-data changes. Only this requested diagnosis file written. Existing unit tests were read, not run.

## Finding

Literal SPACE is preserved in the current piped character-input path. The concrete harness defect is that an input producing zero stdout bytes cannot resolve, even if the interpreter has returned to an input read. Suppression of an unchanged upper-window menu makes this a plausible normal outcome after dismissing menu text. This explains the recorded pattern without requiring SPACE to be lost, but the precise post-SPACE VM state of the three sessions is not proven.

## Exact input path

- [play_broker.py:43](/work/experiments/lanthorn-recall-training/scripts/play_broker.py:43) launches central zvm-cli with `--plain`, pipes and `TERM=dumb`. At lines 92–98 validation does not strip whitespace: command `" "` writes bytes `20 0a`, while command `""` writes `0a`. Literal word `SPACE` would write that word, not a key encoding.
- [main.rs:2195](/work/reference-code/lanthorn/crates/zvm-cli/src/main.rs:2195) routes NeedChar to `read_cooked_char` with plain menus enabled. [main.rs:1061](/work/reference-code/lanthorn/crates/zvm-cli/src/main.rs:1061) reads a whole line, optionally handles host menu commands, then passes the original line to `read_char_from_line` at line 1083.
- [menu.rs:509](/work/reference-code/lanthorn/crates/cli-host/src/menu.rs:509) trims only a local borrowed view for numeric menu selection. An empty/space-only value returns Passthrough; it does not modify the original line. Numeric selection is special: it navigates to the numbered item, and a separate empty Enter selects it.
- [input.rs:70](/work/reference-code/lanthorn/crates/cli-host/src/input.rs:70) removes only CR/LF suffixes, then returns the first byte, defaulting to 13. Thus `" \n"` returns 32, `"\n"` returns 13, and `"SPACE\n"` returns uppercase S (83). The appended newline is consumed as part of the same line, not left behind as a second Enter. Existing tests at lines 143–164 cover Enter and ordinary first-byte behavior, but do not explicitly assert a space.
- Ordinary NeedLine is different: [main.rs:1262](/work/reference-code/lanthorn/crates/zvm-cli/src/main.rs:1262) returns the whole line and terminator 13, then [main.rs:2159](/work/reference-code/lanthorn/crates/zvm-cli/src/main.rs:2159) calls `supply_line(line.trim_end(), terminator)`. All-space line input becomes an empty command. A transcript prompt alone is not an opcode-level input-mode receipt.
- Host paging is disabled by `!mode.plain()` at [main.rs:1783](/work/reference-code/lanthorn/crates/zvm-cli/src/main.rs:1783). These recorded SPACE notices are not the CLI's host pager. Story-authored character prompts remain active.

The central on-disk binary contains `cli_host::input::read_char_from_line`; read-only disassembly at 0x5a9e80 shows the CR/LF-only trim arguments, first-byte extraction and fallback 13. This supports the source mapping for that binary; it does not prove every running process uses that inode/build. Binary SHA256: `f2c88dcdfc97c698304b56a5879526d6eac9b84856ea116135ac295320a97bda`.

